course: dictionary
lesson: 302
title: Doctor words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from hospital stories and science lessons. You can work out much of an unfamiliar word by reading the words around it. «Before an operation the anaesthetist, a doctor whose whole job is keeping you safe asleep, gives you a general anaesthetic.» The sentence tells you the anaesthetist is a doctor, and that the job is keeping you safe while you are asleep.
explain: Look at the word parts too. An anaesthetic is the medicine, and an anaesthetist is the person who gives it. The ending -ist often means a person who does a job, like a dentist or a pianist.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try "a doctor who gives medicine so you feel no pain" in place of anaesthetist. The sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: An anaesthetist is a doctor who gives patients anaesthetic medicine.
fact: Anaesthetic medicine stops patients feeling pain, or makes them fully asleep, during an operation.
fact: An anaesthetist watches over the patient until they wake up.
fact: «Anaesthetist» is used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand; in the USA the word is «anesthesiologist».
fact: In the USA, a nurse who gives anaesthetic is called a nurse anesthetist.
exercise: «An anaesthetist gives the anaesthetic by mask or through a cannula, and watches the patient throughout the operation.» What is the anaesthetist's main job? | Cooking lunch for the nurses | Driving the patient home | *Giving medicine so the patient feels no pain, and watching over them | Cleaning the operating room floor
exercise: The sentence says a cannula is «a thin plastic tube in a vein». What is a cannula? | A small bag of sweets | A bandage for a cut knee | *A thin plastic tube put into a vein | A type of face mask
exercise: «Before an operation the anaesthetist... gives you a general anaesthetic.» What does operation mean here? | A maths sum | A rehearsal for a school play | A quick game of tag | *A medical treatment where doctors work inside the body
test: In the USA, what is an anaesthetist called? | A surgeon | *An anesthesiologist | A pharmacist | A dentist
test: Who keeps a patient safe while they are asleep during an operation? | A bus driver | A postman | A cleaner | *An anaesthetist
exam: «An anaesthetist gives the anaesthetic by mask or through a cannula.» What is the anaesthetist's main job? | *To keep the patient safe and free from pain during an operation | To teach children to read | To cut hair in a salon | To sell medicine in a shop
